{"skill":{"slug":"security-scanner","displayName":"Security Scanner"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770664602049,"changelog":"Initial release - nmap, nuclei, SSL scanning","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1509,"sha256":"2fec659361f60494e6b4695efb7d8f2ff582981f1719b3c7266f10fd6b534cd0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1814,"sha256":"b9ec744de7f7b4d56f3f010f9fd894cb083ed05bda383f6aa4b9bef5b0bcc1e5","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789055608371,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a503b07c0fbc291d562ac4cd7e384d246341f33d4b3c558529f9531e53695a58","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a503b07c0fbc291d562ac4cd7e384d246341f33d4b3c558529f9531e53695a58","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: security-scanner\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle defines a security scanner that utilizes common, legitimate security tools such as nmap, nuclei, sslscan, nikto, and testssl.sh. The instructions in SKILL.md are clear, directly align with the stated purpose of vulnerability scanning, and include ethical guidelines for responsible use. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts designed to subvert the agent for harmful activities. The network and file access are inherent to the functionality of a security scanning tool.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162519793},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":36,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789055608371},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"medium","summary":"This is a simple security-scanning instruction skill that is dual-use but disclosed and purpose-aligned, with no hidden code, persistence, or credential handling.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The commands are active network probes and include full-port and web vulnerability scans, so users should scope targets carefully even though the behavior is expected for a security-scanning skill.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No installer, dependency file, executable script, remote payload retrieval, or package mutation mechanism was present; metadata.json is empty.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill includes an Ethics section requiring authorized targets and written permission, but that constraint appears at the end rather than as an upfront gating step before active scans.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact does not request persistence, elevated privileges, local credential access, background agents, or cross-session state changes.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact describes security scanning and vulnerability assessment, and its nmap, nuclei, nikto, sslscan, and testssl.sh examples directly match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend to use it for systems you own or are explicitly authorized to test. Before running the example scans, define the exact target scope, get permission, and use conservative scan settings for fragile or production systems.","findings":"[YR4] expected: References to offensive or security tools are present, but they are the core documented capability of this security-scanner skill and are not hidden or bundled as executable payloads.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad activation language is a real scoping weakness for a dual-use scanner, but the artifact also explicitly says to scan only authorized targets and get written permission, so this is guidance-level rather than enough for Review by itself.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The skill does not prominently warn that active probes may be detectable or disruptive; that should be considered before use, but the commands are manual examples and there is no automatic execution.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789055608371}}}}}